Z||000000||LottaBallsCamaro||04-30-2001||11:14 PM||||OK, my cousin just wrecked her oldsmobile ciera(80's style) with a brand new 3.8 in it and I'm going to try to convince him to swap it into a fiero. I have done a serch and cannot find any in depth instructions on it to show him what is involved. Could someone help me or point me in the right direction? Hey, I might not be able to own a Fiero, but at least I can work on one then  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"> Oh yeah, we are going to do this swap ourselves as he owns his own shop...||||reg||1
Z||000001||Galen||04-30-2001||11:31 PM||||Are you sure it may not burn up on ya? Of course then you could tell all ya thirdgen friends that their fbodies arn't the only ones who burn up. What a suprise.. You really have got a lotta balls to talk junk about our cars then talk good about em. You put a bad face on fbody and fiero owners.<P>------------------<BR>Galen - 1988 Hawaiian Orchid Coupe - <A HREF="http://myfiero.spinrpg.com/" TARGET=_blank>My Fiero Website</A><BR><A HREF="http://www.spinrpg.com/" TARGET=_blank>Spinrpg.com - Free URL & e-mail Forwarding</A>||||reg||1
Z||000002||fropuff||04-30-2001||11:45 PM|||| <A HREF="http://www.ipass.net/~fieroman/terranexus//fieroman/swap.htm" TARGET=_blank>http://www.ipass.net/~fieroman/terranexus//fieroman/swap.htm</A> <BR> <A HREF="http://members.home.net/gene-down/whatidid.htm" TARGET=_blank>http://members.home.net/gene-down/whatidid.htm</A> <BR> <A HREF="http://www.americancustomeng.com/Engine-Conv.htm" TARGET=_blank>http://www.americancustomeng.com/Engine-Conv.htm</A> <P><BR>Just do it man!<P>------------------<BR>Fuzz busters are for those who are worried about being caught.<p>[This message has been edited by fropuff (edited 04-30-2001).]||||reg||1
Z||000003||Pontiaddict||04-30-2001||11:54 PM||||I'll tell you this one more time.<BR>go here: <A HREF="http://www.angelfire.com/biz/fierosails/info.html" TARGET=_blank>http://www.angelfire.com/biz/fierosails/info.html</A> <BR>bookmark it this time, look here if you want to find info on Fiero stuff.<P>80's doesn't discribe much about the car. Cierra makes me think it's FWD though. If it's rear wheel drive, you'll need an adapter plate. Other than that, swapping motors is basically the same for any kind of motor, it will need new mounts, a way to get the water and fuel lines hooked up, if it is a manual trans fiero getting the motor, it needs a manual trans flywhel. I think chris west sells one for the 3800. Get the wiring diagrams for both cars before doing a compiter swap. I'm just naming things off the top of my head, so don't think of this as the do all instructions for the swap.||||reg||1
